docs {
  # Pagination parameter tests (ONEROSTER-112)

  Covers `limit` / `offset` handling on collection endpoints:

  - valid values are honored, absent values fall back to the default page size (100)
  - a `limit` above the configured ceiling is clamped, not rejected
  - malformed values return HTTP 400 in the `imsx_*` envelope rather than a 500 or a
    silently wrong result set
  - `fetch all pages` walks `offset` until the view is drained, proving the whole
    collection is reachable no matter how low the ceiling is set

  All requests target `users` because the seed data is large enough to page through.

  ## Page-size ceiling

  The API caps a single response at `MAX_PAGE_SIZE` (500 when unset). The E2E env
  files raise it to 20000 so the per-endpoint `list` requests can pull an entire view
  in one call, and the Bruno environments expose the same value as `maxPageSize` so
  the clamp assertion stays in sync. If you change `MAX_PAGE_SIZE` for the API under
  test, the Bruno environment picks it up automatically - both read
  `process.env.MAX_PAGE_SIZE`.

  `fetch all pages` deliberately uses a small page size (100) so it exercises the
  paging loop regardless of the ceiling, and stops after 200 pages as a safety valve.
}
